  "journals": [
    {
      "id": "becoming",
      "title": "The beauty of becoming",
      "label": "THE POINT OF VIEW",
      "excerpt": "A wardrobe is a conversation with the person you are becoming.",
      "image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/hr5xa7o9/image/upload/v1793754721/rms/original-hero.jpg",
      "hover": "https://res.cloudinary.com/hr5xa7o9/image/upload/v1793754723/rms/original-portrait.jpg",
      "alt": "Sculptural black dress editorial",
      "body": "Personal style is rarely a destination. More often, it is a practice of noticing what feels like you.\n\nSome days call for a clear, sculptural line. Others need a little softness, a familiar shape or a colour that shifts your mood. A considered wardrobe makes space for all of those versions of yourself.\n\n## Less noise. More you.\n\nBegin with the pieces you reach for instinctively. Notice their proportions, textures and the way they move. Let these become the foundation, then add something unexpected: a stronger silhouette, a new shade, a detail that makes you look twice.\n\nThe most lasting style is personal. It is not about arriving at a finished version of yourself. It is about enjoying the becoming.",
      "status": "published",
      "featured": true,
      "readMinutes": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "structure",
      "title": "A study in soft structure",
      "label": "THE WARDROBE",
      "excerpt": "On the quiet power of a beautifully considered silhouette.",
      "image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/hr5xa7o9/image/upload/v1793754717/rms/original-cream.jpg",
      "hover": "https://res.cloudinary.com/hr5xa7o9/image/upload/v1793754724/rms/original-suit.jpg",
      "alt": "Relaxed neutral tailoring",
      "body": "There is a particular kind of confidence in clothes that never need to announce themselves.\n\nA generous sleeve. A shoulder with just enough definition. The way a trouser falls when you take a step. These small decisions shape how a garment lives with you, and how you feel within it.\n\n## Room to move\n\nSoft tailoring begins with balance: structure without stiffness, ease without losing intention. Wear a full set for a composed silhouette, or separate the pieces and let each find its own rhythm.\n\nThe result is a wardrobe that works with you. For the planned moments, and the ones that happen in between.",
      "status": "published",
      "featured": true,
      "readMinutes": 3
    }
  ]
}
